{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","title":"lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":744,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:integral-curve-exists]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","line":1089,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Vanishing differential at a local maximum]\n\\label{lem:differential-vanishes-at-max}\n\n\n\nIf a smooth $f\\colon M\\to\\Ar$ has a local maximum at $q$, then\n$df_q=0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:integral-curve-exists}\nExtend any $v\\in T_qM$ to a smooth field and evaluate $f$ along its\nintegral curve through $q$. Fermat's lemma gives $df_q(v)=0$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Vanishing differential at a local maximum] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a646966666572656e7469616c2d76616e69736865732d61742d6d6178\"></span> <p></p>If a smooth <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f\\colon M\\to \\Ar $\">$f\\colon M\\to \\Ar $</span> has a local maximum at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$df_q=0$\">$df_q=0$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aintegral-curve-exists\">↗ lem:integral-curve-exists</a> Extend any <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in T_qM$\">$v\\in T_qM$</span> to a smooth field and evaluate <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> along its integral curve through <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span>. Fermat’s lemma gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$df_q(v)=0$\">$df_q(v)=0$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:integral-curve-exists","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:integral-curve-exists","title":"lem:integral-curve-exists","label":"lem:integral-curve-exists"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max","title":"lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max","label":"lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","title":"lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","label":"lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","title":"lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Vanishing differential at a local maximum]\n\\label{lem:differential-vanishes-at-max}\n\n\n\nIf a smooth $f\\colon M\\to\\Ar$ has a local maximum at $q$, then\n$df_q=0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{l